    audio: 'Remote computer audio', ask: 'Ask for the options when connecting', connect_options: 'Options for this session:',
    mic: 'This computer’s microphone on the remote one',
    mic_denied: 'The browser does not allow the microphone: allow it for this page (icon next to the address) so the remote computer can hear you.',
    mic_https: 'The microphone only works when the page is opened with https:// (or on the server’s own computer).',
    mic_none: 'No microphone was found on this computer.', mic_unsupported: 'This browser cannot send the microphone.',
    mic_failed: 'The microphone of this computer could not be opened.',
    more_info: 'More information',
    mic_info_browser_h: 'The browser asks for permission',
    mic_info_browser: 'The first time a program of the remote computer uses the microphone (a call, a dictation, Windows’ microphone test), the browser asks whether this page may use it: press “Allow”. If you block it, change it later with the icon next to the address. While it records, the browser shows its own sign. It only works when the page is opened with https:// (or on the server’s own computer).',
    mic_info_server_h: 'On the remote computer (Windows)',
    mic_info_server: 'Windows 10 and 11 allow audio recording over Remote Desktop as they come: the session shows a microphone called “Remote Audio”. If it does not, a policy forbids it. As an administrator on the remote computer, allow it in one of these two ways:',
    mic_info_gpo_h: 'With the policy editor (an MMC console)',
    mic_info_gpo: ['Press Windows + R, type gpedit.msc and press Enter.',
      'Go to Computer Configuration → Administrative Templates → Windows Components → Remote Desktop Services → Remote Desktop Session Host → Device and Resource Redirection.',
      'Open “Allow audio recording redirection”, choose “Enabled” and press OK.',
      'Run gpupdate /force to apply it.'],
    mic_info_reg_h: 'With the registry',
    mic_info_reg: 'In a command prompt opened as an administrator (/d 0 allows it; /d 1 forbids it):',
    mic_info_service: 'On Windows Server, its Windows Audio service must be running as well (in PowerShell opened as an administrator):',
    mic_info_after: 'Then sign out of the remote session (disconnecting is not enough) and connect again with this box ticked.',
    screens_info_this_h: 'In this browser', screens_info_other_h: 'In other browsers',
    screens_info_api: 'Chrome and Edge: the first time, the browser asks whether this page may manage windows on all your displays: press “Allow”. Without that permission only this screen is used. If you block it, change it later with the icon next to the address.',
    screens_info_popup: 'Firefox and Safari do not list the screens: the other one is looked for by opening a window next to this one, and the browser may block it as a pop-up. Allow pop-ups for this site (the notice shows next to the address bar). When the other screen is on the left, the first time that window has to be taken to it. Safari has not been tested.',
    screens_info_general: 'Each screen is a separate monitor of the remote computer while its window is open; closing it removes that monitor without reconnecting.',
    remember_opts: 'Remember these options and do not ask again', mute: 'Mute', unmute: 'Unmute',
    paste_typing: 'Phone keyboard through the clipboard', paste_auto: 'Automatic (on for phones and tablets)', paste_on: 'Always', paste_off: 'Never',
    paste_info: 'Why this option exists',
    paste_info_problem: 'When typing with the on-screen keyboard of a phone or tablet, Windows 11 Notepad, Terminal and Explorer garble the text: they repeat the last letter of a word, drop capitals or letters and sometimes an Enter. WordPad, Word, browsers and Windows search receive it fine, and the physical keyboard is not affected. It is a Windows 11 bug that other programs describe too; Microsoft has not fixed it.',
    paste_info_cause_h: 'Why it happens',
    paste_info_cause: 'RDP can only send text as Unicode letters or as keys, and Microsoft\'s Windows App uses the same two ways. Measured on Windows 11 Pro: Notepad\'s spell check and autocorrection go through the text in the background and drop a key when another control key or a paste arrives right behind it. Windows gives no sign of when they are done, so no client can wait for them exactly.',
    paste_info_what_h: 'What the option does',
    paste_info_what: 'Text the keyboard sends in one go (autocorrection, swipe typing, dictation) is pasted through the Windows clipboard, and each step waits for a sign from Windows. Whatever you had copied in Windows (text, formatting, images) is read first and put back afterwards, without showing in the history (Win+V); if it was files, the text is typed instead of pasted. Single letters go as before. In programs where Ctrl+V is not paste (PuTTY, vim), untick it.',
    paste_info_tests_h: 'Tests',
    paste_info_tests: 'In Windows 11 Pro Notepad, over RDP from MuDeskClient, with 76-character lines (accents, ñ, ¿?, €, @ and capitals) sent word by word, as a phone sends them:',
    paste_info_rows: [['Unicode letters, one every 100 ms, with spell check', '1 of 3 lines wrong'], ['The same, without spell check', '3 of 3 right'],
      ['Keys of the layout, at a person\'s pace', '1 of 3 wrong'], ['Keys of the layout, all at once', '3 of 3 wrong'],
      ['Pasting the text through the clipboard', '8 of 8 right'], ['Enter with a letter right behind', '0 of 18 lost'],
      ['Enter with a paste right behind, with spell check', '3 of 8 lost'], ['The same, without spell check', '0 of 8 lost'],
      ['Real pace: 0.3 s to the Enter and 0.4 s to the next word, with spell check', 'text 24 of 24 right; Enters 22 of 24'],
      ['Two pastes in a row (the clipboard is put back after each)', '21 of 21 right in the Run box; 30 of 30 words in Notepad']],
    paste_info_tip: 'If you type a lot from a phone in Notepad, turn off Settings → Spelling → "Spell check" and "Autocorrect" in it.',
    paste_info_sources_h: 'Sources',
    paste_info_sources: ['nemo-voice-typing #4: dictated text garbled in Notepad and Terminal', 'dictatem #278: text garbled in Windows 11 Notepad',
      'nectarlink #288: keys of the layout instead of Unicode letters', 'relay #20: typing into Windows 11 Notepad',
      'justrdp #532: the Windows 11 24H2 console drops Unicode letters over RDP', 'Microsoft: Windows App keyboard modes (Unicode or scancode)'],
    paste_hint: 'For connecting to Windows 11 from a phone or tablet: Notepad, Terminal and Explorer mix up the letters the on-screen keyboard sends together. That text is pasted through the Windows clipboard, which is then left as it was. Needs the shared clipboard.',
